{"id": "18e91267241b2313a404b47cd640cfeeb900a2c1", "candidate_id": "bennett", "candidate_name": "Juliana Bennett", "collector": "wi_outlet_wkow", "title": "Pat Weiler Becomes 76th Member of AEM Hall of Fame", "text": "The Weiler founder accepted the honor Nov. 12, 2026, at the AEM Annual Conference in Tucson, Arizona", "source": "WKOW 27", "source_url": "https://www.wkow.com/online_features/press_releases/pat-weiler-becomes-76th-member-of-aem-hall-of-fame/article_bf0a7c28-1138-5643-b89b-acfce1963d16.html", "resolved_url": "https://www.wkow.com/online_features/press_releases/pat-weiler-becomes-76th-member-of-aem-hall-of-fame/article_bf0a7c28-1138-5643-b89b-acfce1963d16.html", "url_resolution": "direct", "text_source": "collector", "full_text_status": "fetch_failed:HTTPError", "published_at": "2026-11-13T19:59:00+00:00", "reason": "no_name_match"}
{"id": "d1670fccfd9036ebbb72b0e1be54d65adacacb6c", "candidate_id": "martinez_rutherford", "candidate_name": "Dina Nina Martinez Rutherford", "collector": "wi_outlet_wkow", "title": "Pat Weiler Becomes 76th Member of AEM Hall of Fame", "text": "The Weiler founder accepted the honor Nov. 12, 2026, at the AEM Annual Conference in Tucson, Arizona MILWAUKEE , Nov. 13, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Pat Weiler, founder of Weiler and a leader in equipment engineering and manufacturing for more than 45 years, joined the Association of Equipment Manufacturers (AEM) Hall of Fame as its 2026 inductee. Weiler accepted the honor Nov. 12, 2026, in front of his industry peers and family at the AEM Annual Conference in Tucson, Arizona. \"AEM is the preeminent voice and leading advocate for equipment manufacturers, representing an industry that is critical to our economy and global competitiveness,\" said Weiler. \"I am truly honored to accept this award from such a respected and influential organization.\" The AEM Hall of Fame recognizes individuals whose leadership and contributions have shaped the equipment manufacturing industry. Weiler earned the recognition for decades of product innovation, industry leadership and philanthropy that have strengthened customers, employees and communities. \"Congratulations to Pat on this well-deserved honor,\" said AEM President and CEO Megan Tanel. \"Pat has spent his career solving real problems for customers, and his innovations have raised the bar for equipment design across our industry. His leadership has strengthened our collective voice, and his generosity through the Weiler Foundation shows what it truly means to invest in people and communities. Our industry is stronger because of Pat Weiler.\" About Pat Weiler With more than 45 years of engineering, manufacturing and customer-focused leadership, Pat Weiler has built a career defined by innovation, entrepreneurship and service. Pat founded Weiler in 2000 and the company has grown under his leadership to a significant manufacturing organization and one of the largest employers in Marion County, Iowa. Weiler Forestry was added in 2019; Pat now leads manufacturing operations in multiple markets and states. Driven by a commitment to solving customers' real-world challenges, Weiler has earned 10 U.S. patents, with additional patents pending, and become the market-share leader in material transfer vehicles, road wideners and windrow elevators. The Weiler P385C commercial paver has grown to be the highest-selling model of its kind in North America since its 2009 introduction and helped reshape industry design standards. Pat has continued to diversify the business through strategic acquisitions, including a top-hammer rock drill product line in 2017, a purpose-built forestry product line division in 2019 and a self-propelled broom in 2024. Pat's impact extends well beyond the manufacturing floor. A member of the AEM Board of Directors and past chair of the AEM PAC, he has been recognized with the 2019 AEM Pillar of the Industry Award, AEM's Advocacy Gold Award from 2020 through 2025, the 2026 Alan Curtis Industry Service Award, and the Legend in Manufacturing Award from the Iowa Association of Business and Industry. He was also inducted into the Pavement Hall of Fame in 2026. Through the Weiler Foundation, Pat supports local organizations with annual grants and donations, including a recent $5 million commitment to the local hospital. He has championed affordable housing initiatives and helped establish one of Iowa's first registered apprenticeship programs, which became a model across the state. His leadership reflects a guiding belief: the business decisions made today should support customers, strengthen employees, their families and the communities they call home. About the AEM Hall of Fame The AEM Hall of Fame honors the pioneers who have invented, managed, built and led the nonroad equipment manufacturing industry across the agriculture, construction, forestry, mining and utility sectors. The program traces its roots to 1993 and the Construction Equipment Hall of Fame, launched by Construction Equipment magazine. AEM took over ownership and operation of the program in 2008. An independent panel of industry experts evaluates each nominee on four guiding principles: innovation, industry contributions, leadership and corporate citizenship/social responsibility. AEM accepts nominations year-round. To explore past inductees, submit a nomination or learn more about the program, visit the AEM Hall of Fame website . About AEM The Association of Equipment Manufacturers (AEM) is the North American-based international trade group representing nonroad equipment manufacturers and suppliers, with more than 1,100 companies and more than 200 product lines in the agriculture and construction-related industry sectors worldwide. The equipment manufacturing industry in the United States supports over 2.2 million jobs and contributes $415 billion to the economy every year. View original content to download multimedia: https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/pat-weiler-becomes-76th-member-of-aem-hall-of-fame-302939300.html SOURCE Association of Equipment Manufacturers (AEM)", "source": "WKOW 27", "source_url": "https://www.wkow.com/online_features/press_releases/pat-weiler-becomes-76th-member-of-aem-hall-of-fame/article_bf0a7c28-1138-5643-b89b-acfce1963d16.html", "resolved_url": "https://www.wkow.com/online_features/press_releases/pat-weiler-becomes-76th-member-of-aem-hall-of-fame/article_bf0a7c28-1138-5643-b89b-acfce1963d16.html", "url_resolution": "direct", "text_source": "full_text", "full_text_status": "ok", "published_at": "2026-11-13T19:59:00+00:00", "reason": "no_name_match"}
