{"id": "c3920a15704f1b6c0246a37403b60c6bde91e245", "candidate_id": "bennett", "candidate_name": "Juliana Bennett", "collector": "wi_outlet_channel3000", "title": "New candidate enters race for District 15", "text": "MADISON, Wis. — A new candidate is vying for a seat on the Madison Common Council for District 15 alder. Ryan Koglin has announced his candidacy. The seat is currently held by Dina Nina Martinez-Rutherford, who was recently elected to represent District 76 in the Wisconsin State Legislature. Koglin previously ran for the District 15 seat in 2025. Although Martinez-Rutherford dropped out of that race after her name was already printed on the ballot, she still won the election by 219 votes, deciding then to remain in that seat. Koglin holds a master’s degree in marriage and family therapy and is currently self-employed, running a local dog-hiking business. The general election will take place on April 7, with a primary scheduled for February, if necessary. ​COPYRIGHT 2026 BY CHANNEL 3000. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. THIS MATERIAL MAY NOT BE PUBLISHED, BROADCAST, REWRITTEN OR REDISTRIBUTED.", "source": "Channel 3000 / WISC-TV", "source_url": "https://www.channel3000.com/news/new-candidate-enters-race-for-district-15/article_1e35b42c-d3c8-45d7-8d30-1a1bba3bd050.html", "resolved_url": "https://www.channel3000.com/news/new-candidate-enters-race-for-district-15/article_1e35b42c-d3c8-45d7-8d30-1a1bba3bd050.html", "url_resolution": "direct", "text_source": "full_text", "full_text_status": "ok", "published_at": "2026-11-16T21:06:00+00:00", "reason": "failed_double_check"}
